# Files still reading a gated service-address config key as a literal, rather than resolving
# through Sorcha.ServiceClients.Configuration.SorchaServiceAddresses.
#
# RATCHET: may only shrink. A stale entry (file no longer carrying such a literal) fails the gate,
# so an entry must be removed in the same PR that removes the literal.
#
# What is on this list, and why it is lower priority than what was fixed:
#   Every entry below reads the CANONICAL spelling (ServiceClients:{X}Service:Address) with its own
#   local default. They are consistent with each other — they had not drifted. What DID drift, and
#   what DRIFT-006 fixed, was the Tenant Service address: six call sites each hand-rolling a
#   different fallback chain over four different spellings, so which key a deployment had to set
#   depended on which client resolved it. Those are all migrated and none appear here.
#   These remaining sites still gain from the resolver (a deployment using a legacy spelling would
#   not reach them), so the list shrinks over time — but none of them is a live inconsistency.
#
# The API Gateway is deliberately NOT gated at all: its `Services:{X}:Url` section is its own
# namespace for the aggregation views, is what compose sets for that container, and is already
# accepted by the resolver as a fallback spelling.
